# The repo always stores LF, and checkout keeps LF on Windows too. This harness
# is developed on Win11 and Ubuntu: without this, a commit from Windows can
# rewrite files to CRLF and pollute every diff. `.nvmrc` is the critical case —
# with CRLF, `node-version-file` in the workflows and the fnm/nvm auto-switch
# both read "24\r".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts: they need CRLF to run correctly.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
